sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2025-wisdom-12> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Normal brain morphogenesis in vertebrate (frog) embryos depends on a specific bioelectric prepattern that chemical or genetic teratogens alter; forcing a return to the correct prepattern in the neural plate, for example by activating the HCN2 channel, corrects brain morphology, gene expression and learning capacity in animals exposed to alcohol, nicotine or a dominant Notch mutation.";
    dc:type "experimental-result";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Restoring the neural-plate bioelectric prepattern rescues teratogen and Notch defects";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “The Multiscale Wisdom of the Body: Collective Intelligence as a Tractable Interface for Next-Generation Biomedicine”, BioEssays : news and reviews in molecular, cellular and developmental biology (2025), doi:10.1002/bies.202400196; section “Bioelectricity as the Interface to Multicellularity › Birth Defect Repair and Limb Regeneration”. Scope: Xenopus laevis embryos exposed to alcohol, nicotine or Notch mutation (author's lab's prior work, refs [124–126])"
}
